msgid "**Resource Pool** — Select the cluster resource pool"
msgstr "**Resource Pool** — Selecione o pool de recursos do cluster"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:158
msgid "**VLAN ID** — The native VLAN ID for the network"
msgstr "**VLAN ID** — O ID de VLAN nativa para a rede"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:159
msgid ""
"**VLAN Trunks** — Comma-separated list of trunk VLAN IDs or ranges (for "
"example, ``100,200-210``)"
msgstr ""
"**VLAN Trunks** — Lista separada por vírgulas de IDs de VLAN trunk ou "
"intervalos (por exemplo, ``100,200-210``)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:160
msgid "**Trunk Only** — Enable to use trunk-only mode (no native VLAN)"
msgstr "**Trunk Only** — Habilite para utilizar o modo trunk-only (sem VLAN nativa)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:165
msgid "VLAN Modes and Traffic Behavior"
msgstr "Modos de VLAN e Comportamento de Tráfego"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:167
msgid "Standard Networks support three VLAN modes based on configuration:"
msgstr "As Redes Standard suportam três modos de VLAN com base na configuração:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:169
msgid "**Access Mode (Default)**"
msgstr "**Modo Access (Padrão)**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:171
msgid ""
"The OVS bridge handles VLAN tagging transparently. The VM receives "
"untagged Ethernet frames and remains unaware of VLAN assignments."
msgstr ""
"A bridge OVS gerencia a marcação de VLAN de forma transparente. A VM recebe "
"quadros Ethernet sem tag e permanece sem conhecimento das atribuições de VLAN."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:173
msgid "UI fields: VLAN ID = 200, VLAN Trunks = (empty), Trunk Only = off"
msgstr "Campos da UI: VLAN ID = 200, VLAN Trunks = (vazio), Trunk Only = off"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:174
msgid ""
"Egress (VM → network): The VM sends an untagged frame, and the OVS bridge"
" inserts the VLAN 200 tag before forwarding to the uplink"
msgstr ""
"Saída (VM → rede): A VM envia um quadro sem tag e a bridge OVS insere a "
"tag VLAN 200 antes de encaminhar para o uplink"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:175
msgid ""
"Ingress (network → VM): OVS receives a VLAN 200 tagged frame, removes the"
" tag, and delivers an untagged frame to the VM"
msgstr ""
"Entrada (rede → VM): O OVS recebe um quadro com tag VLAN 200, remove a "
"tag e entrega um quadro sem tag para a VM"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:177
msgid "**Hybrid Mode (Native VLAN + Trunk VLANs)**"
msgstr "**Modo Hybrid (VLAN Nativa + VLANs Trunk)**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:179
msgid ""
"The system uses VLAN 0 as an untagged passthrough marker in the port "
"group XML. The untagged traffic uses the native VLAN and trunk VLANs pass"
" through tagged."
msgstr ""
"O sistema utiliza VLAN 0 como marcador de passagem sem tag no XML do port "
"group. O tráfego sem tag utiliza a VLAN nativa e as VLANs trunk passam "
"com tag."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:181
msgid "UI fields: VLAN ID = 200, VLAN Trunks = 100,300, Trunk Only = off"
msgstr "Campos da UI: VLAN ID = 200, VLAN Trunks = 100,300, Trunk Only = off"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:182
msgid ""
"The VM can send/receive both untagged (native VLAN 200) and tagged (VLANs"
" 100, 300) traffic"
msgstr ""
"A VM pode enviar/receber tráfego sem tag (VLAN nativa 200) e com tag "
"(VLANs 100, 300)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:184
msgid "**Trunk-Only Mode**"
msgstr "**Modo Trunk-Only**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:186
msgid "All traffic is tagged. No native VLAN is assigned."
msgstr "Todo o tráfego possui tag. Nenhuma VLAN nativa é atribuída."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:188
msgid "UI fields: VLAN ID = (any), VLAN Trunks = 100,200,300, Trunk Only = on"
msgstr "Campos da UI: VLAN ID = (qualquer), VLAN Trunks = 100,200,300, Trunk Only = on"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:189
msgid ""
"The VM must tag all outgoing frames and expects all incoming frames to be"
" tagged"
msgstr ""
"A VM deve marcar todos os quadros de saída e espera que todos os quadros "
"de entrada possuam tag"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:192
msgid "Modifying an HVM Standard Network"
msgstr "Modificando uma Rede HVM Standard"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:194
msgid ""
"You can modify the **VLAN Trunks** and **Trunk Only** fields on an "
"existing Standard Network after creation. You cannot modify the VLAN ID, "
"Resource Pool, or Router fields."
msgstr ""
"Você pode modificar os campos **VLAN Trunks** e **Trunk Only** em uma "
"Rede Standard existente após a criação. Não é possível modificar os campos "
"VLAN ID, Resource Pool ou Router."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:197
msgid "Select the Standard Network to modify"
msgstr "Selecione a Rede Standard a ser modificada"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:198
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Edit`"
msgstr "Clique em :guilabel:`Edit`"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:199
msgid "Modify the following fields:"
msgstr "Modifique os seguintes campos:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:201
msgid ""
"**VLAN Trunks** — Update the comma-separated list of trunk VLAN IDs or "
"ranges. The system provisions added VLANs on all hosts and removes "
"deleted VLANs unless another network in the same cluster and OVS bridge "
"still uses them."
msgstr ""
"**VLAN Trunks** — Atualize a lista separada por vírgulas de IDs de VLAN "
"trunk ou intervalos. O sistema provisiona as VLANs adicionadas em todos os "
"hosts e remove as VLANs excluídas, a menos que outra rede no mesmo cluster "
"e bridge OVS ainda as utilize."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:202
msgid ""
"**Trunk Only** — Toggle trunk-only mode on or off. The system removes the"
" native VLAN tag from the OVS port when switching from Hybrid to Trunk-"
"only, and restores the native VLAN tag when switching back."
msgstr ""
"**Trunk Only** — Alterne o modo trunk-only entre ligado e desligado. O "
"sistema remove a tag de VLAN nativa da porta OVS ao alternar de Hybrid para "
"Trunk-only e restaura a tag de VLAN nativa ao alternar de volta."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:204
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Save Changes`"
msgstr "Clique em :guilabel:`Save Changes`"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:206
msgid "The plugin updates the port group XML on all hosts in the cluster."
msgstr "O plugin atualiza o XML do port group em todos os hosts do cluster."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:209
msgid "Creating HVM Overlay Networks"
msgstr "Criando Redes HVM Overlay"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:211
msgid ""
"An HVM Overlay Network uses VXLAN tunneling to provide isolation for "
"east-west VM traffic across hosts. It enables tenant network segmentation"
" without requiring physical VLAN configuration on upstream switches."
msgstr ""
"Uma Rede HVM Overlay utiliza tunelamento VXLAN para fornecer isolamento "
"para tráfego leste-oeste de VMs entre hosts. Ela permite a segmentação de "
"rede de tenants sem exigir configuração física de VLAN nos switches upstream."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:213
msgid ""
"The system deploys a dedicated OVS bridge for each overlay network on "
"every host and configures a VXLAN tunnel endpoint on a designated host "
"interface."
msgstr ""
"O sistema implanta uma bridge OVS dedicada para cada rede overlay em todos "
"os hosts e configura um endpoint de túnel VXLAN em uma interface de host "
"designada."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:215
msgid ""
"Before creation, verify that every participating host has the selected "
"tunnel interface, that tunnel-endpoint addresses are mutually reachable "
"through the underlay, and that the underlay MTU can carry the additional "
"VXLAN encapsulation without fragmentation. VNI values must be unique "
"within the applicable VXLAN domain. These requirements apply to the "
"legacy/layout 1.3 plugin described on this page; layout 2.0 uses the "
"Virtual Switch model and must not be configured from this workflow."
msgstr ""
"Antes da criação, verifique se todos os hosts participantes possuem a "
"interface de túnel selecionada, se os endereços dos endpoints de túnel são "
"mutuamente acessíveis pela rede underlay e se o MTU da underlay pode "
"transportar o encapsulamento VXLAN adicional sem fragmentação. Os valores "
"de VNI devem ser únicos dentro do domínio VXLAN aplicável. Esses requisitos "
"se aplicam ao plugin legacy/layout 1.3 descrito nesta página; o layout 2.0 "
"utiliza o modelo Virtual Switch e não deve ser configurado a partir deste "
"fluxo de trabalho."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:219
msgid ""
"The HVM Overlay Network does not use the same OVS Bridge Domain virtual "
"switch as Standard Networks. Instead, the system creates a dedicated OVS "
"bridge for each Overlay Network on every host, ensuring complete "
"isolation from other networks."
msgstr ""
"A Rede HVM Overlay não utiliza o mesmo virtual switch OVS Bridge Domain "
"das Redes Standard. Em vez disso, o sistema cria uma bridge OVS dedicada "
"para cada Rede Overlay em todos os hosts, garantindo isolamento completo "
"de outras redes."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:222
msgid "Select :guilabel:`+ Add` > **HVM Overlay Network**"
msgstr "Selecione :guilabel:`+ Add` > **HVM Overlay Network**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:225
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:248
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:266
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:331
msgid "**Group** — Select the group"
msgstr "**Group** — Selecione o grupo"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:228
msgid "**VNI** — The VXLAN Network Identifier for tunnel isolation"
msgstr "**VNI** — O identificador de rede VXLAN para isolamento de túnel"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:229
msgid ""
"**Tunnel Interface** — The host interface used as the VXLAN tunnel "
"endpoint"
msgstr ""
"**Tunnel Interface** — A interface do host utilizada como endpoint do "
"túnel VXLAN"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:234
msgid "Creating HVM Data Networks"
msgstr "Criando Redes HVM Data"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:236
msgid ""
"An HVM Data Network creates a Linux VLAN interface on each host and maps "
"it to a libvirt network. It is designed to handle high-throughput in-"
"guest storage traffic, such as iSCSI or NFS. It also supports MTU "
"configuration for jumbo frames."
msgstr ""
"Uma Rede HVM Data cria uma interface VLAN Linux em cada host e a mapeia "
"para uma rede libvirt. Ela é projetada para lidar com tráfego de "
"armazenamento de alto throughput dentro do guest, como iSCSI ou NFS. Ela "
"também suporta configuração de MTU para jumbo frames."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:240
msgid "You can apply MTU changes only to stopped VMs"
msgstr "Você pode aplicar alterações de MTU somente em VMs paradas"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:241
msgid "Ensure to stop and start each VM after changing the MTU"
msgstr "Certifique-se de parar e iniciar cada VM após alterar o MTU"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:242
msgid ""
"Configure the same MTU inside the guest only when the complete network "
"path is designed and validated for that frame size"
msgstr ""
"Configure o mesmo MTU dentro do guest somente quando o caminho de rede "
"completo estiver projetado e validado para esse tamanho de quadro"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:245
msgid "Select :guilabel:`+ Add` > **HVM Data Network**"
msgstr "Selecione :guilabel:`+ Add` > **HVM Data Network**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:251
msgid "**VLAN ID** — The VLAN for the data network"
msgstr "**VLAN ID** — A VLAN para a rede de dados"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:252
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:270
msgid "**Host Interface** — The host interface for the VLAN sub-interface"
msgstr "**Host Interface** — A interface do host para a sub-interface VLAN"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:253
msgid ""
"**MTU** — Maximum transmission unit. Use ``9000`` only for a validated "
"end-to-end jumbo-frame path; otherwise use the network's standard MTU"
msgstr ""
"**MTU** — Unidade máxima de transmissão. Utilize ``9000`` somente para um "
"caminho de jumbo frame validado de ponta a ponta; caso contrário, utilize "
"o MTU padrão da rede"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:258
msgid "Creating HVM Private Networks"
msgstr "Criando Redes HVM Private"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:260
msgid ""
"The HVM Private Network creates a MacVTAP-backed libvirt network on each "
"host. The system creates a VLAN-tagged sub-interface on the selected host"
" interface using the specified VLAN ID. When a VM connects to this "
"network, libvirt automatically creates a macvtap interface on the host, "
"providing direct connectivity to the physical network segment."
msgstr ""
"A Rede HVM Private cria uma rede libvirt baseada em MacVTAP em cada host. "
"O sistema cria uma sub-interface com tag de VLAN na interface de host "
"selecionada utilizando o ID de VLAN especificado. Quando uma VM se conecta "
"a esta rede, o libvirt cria automaticamente uma interface macvtap no host, "
"fornecendo conectividade direta ao segmento de rede física."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:263
msgid "Select :guilabel:`+ Add` > **HVM Private Network**"
msgstr "Selecione :guilabel:`+ Add` > **HVM Private Network**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:269
msgid "**VLAN ID** — The VLAN for the private network"
msgstr "**VLAN ID** — A VLAN para a rede privada"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:275
msgid "Creating HVM SR-IOV Networks"
msgstr "Criando Redes HVM SR-IOV"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:277
msgid ""
"The HVM SR-IOV Network uses SR-IOV Virtual Functions (VFs) on a physical "
"NIC to deliver near-native network performance. The plugin maps a libvirt"
" hostdev network to a Physical Function (PF), and libvirt manages the "
"assignment of VFs to individual VMs. The NIC hardware performs VLAN "
"Switch Tagging (VST), inserting and removing VLAN tags directly in "
"hardware, making the process transparent to the VM guest OS."
msgstr ""
"A Rede HVM SR-IOV utiliza Virtual Functions (VFs) SR-IOV em uma NIC física "
"para fornecer desempenho de rede quase nativo. O plugin mapeia uma rede "
"libvirt hostdev para uma Physical Function (PF), e o libvirt gerencia a "
"atribuição de VFs a VMs individuais. O hardware da NIC realiza VLAN Switch "
"Tagging (VST), inserindo e removendo tags de VLAN diretamente no hardware, "
"tornando o processo transparente para o SO guest da VM."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:281
msgid "The system does not support live migration of VMs that use SR-IOV networks"
msgstr "O sistema não suporta migração ao vivo de VMs que utilizam redes SR-IOV"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:282
msgid ""
"Ensure that you enable SR-IOV in the host BIOS/UEFI before configuring "
"SR-IOV networks"
msgstr ""
"Certifique-se de habilitar o SR-IOV no BIOS/UEFI do host antes de "
"configurar redes SR-IOV"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:283
msgid ""
"The plugin automatically detects SR-IOV-capable Physical Functions on "
"each host"
msgstr ""
"O plugin detecta automaticamente Physical Functions compatíveis com SR-IOV "
"em cada host"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:287
msgid ""
"Monitor libvirt behavior after VM clone, backup, or restore because VF "
"tracking can become inconsistent. Restart the ``libvirtd`` daemon if VF "
"tracking issues occur."
msgstr ""
"Monitore o comportamento do libvirt após clone, backup ou restauração de "
"VM, pois o rastreamento de VF pode se tornar inconsistente. Reinicie o "
"daemon ``libvirtd`` se ocorrerem problemas de rastreamento de VF."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:290
msgid "Understanding Physical Functions and Virtual Functions"
msgstr "Entendendo Physical Functions e Virtual Functions"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:292
msgid ""
"**Physical Function (PF)** — A full-featured PCIe device on a physical "
"network adapter that manages and controls SR-IOV functionality. The host "
"OS discovers and manages the PF like a standard physical NIC. The PF "
"driver controls the hardware, enables SR-IOV, and creates Virtual "
"Functions."
msgstr ""
"**Physical Function (PF)** — Um dispositivo PCIe completo em um adaptador "
"de rede físico que gerencia e controla a funcionalidade SR-IOV. O SO do "
"host descobre e gerencia a PF como uma NIC física padrão. O driver da PF "
"controla o hardware, habilita o SR-IOV e cria Virtual Functions."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:293
msgid ""
"**Virtual Function (VF)** — A lightweight PCIe function derived from a PF"
" that provides near-native I/O performance to a VM. Each VF operates "
"independently with its own queue and interrupt, allowing direct hardware "
"access without hypervisor overhead."
msgstr ""
"**Virtual Function (VF)** — Uma função PCIe leve derivada de uma PF que "
"fornece desempenho de I/O quase nativo a uma VM. Cada VF opera de forma "
"independente com sua própria fila e interrupção, permitindo acesso direto "
"ao hardware sem sobrecarga do hypervisor."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:296
msgid "AppArmor Configuration"
msgstr "Configuração do AppArmor"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:298
msgid ""
"Configure AppArmor on each host to allow libvirt/QEMU to access VFIO "
"devices for SR-IOV Virtual Functions:"
msgstr ""
"Configure o AppArmor em cada host para permitir que o libvirt/QEMU acesse "
"dispositivos VFIO para Virtual Functions SR-IOV:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:300
msgid ""
"Add the following entry to the local libvirt-qemu AppArmor abstraction "
"file:"
msgstr ""
"Adicione a seguinte entrada ao arquivo de abstração AppArmor local do "
"libvirt-qemu:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:302
msgid ""
"# File: /etc/apparmor.d/local/abstractions/libvirt-qemu\n"
"# Allow read/write/lock access to all VFIO group devices for SR-IOV VFs\n"
"/dev/vfio/* krw,"
msgstr ""
"# Arquivo: /etc/apparmor.d/local/abstractions/libvirt-qemu\n"
"# Permitir acesso de leitura/escrita/bloqueio a todos os dispositivos de grupo VFIO para VFs SR-IOV\n"
"/dev/vfio/* krw,"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:308
msgid "Reload AppArmor after making the change:"
msgstr "Recarregue o AppArmor após fazer a alteração:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:310
msgid "sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/abstractions/libvirt-qemu"
msgstr "sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/abstractions/libvirt-qemu"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:315
msgid "Host NIC VF Management"
msgstr "Gerenciamento de VF de NIC do Host"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:317
msgid ""
"When you create an SR-IOV network, the plugin automatically performs the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"Quando você cria uma rede SR-IOV, o plugin realiza automaticamente o "
"seguinte:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:319
msgid ""
"Discovers all SR-IOV-capable Physical Functions (PFs) on each host by "
"reading ``/sys/class/net/*/device/sriov_totalvfs``"
msgstr ""
"Descobre todas as Physical Functions (PFs) compatíveis com SR-IOV em cada "
"host lendo ``/sys/class/net/*/device/sriov_totalvfs``"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:320
msgid ""
"If Virtual Functions (VFs) are not enabled, the plugin installs and "
"starts a persistent systemd service on the host. This service writes "
"``sriov_totalvfs`` to ``sriov_numvfs``, ensuring VFs remain enabled "
"across reboots."
msgstr ""
"Se as Virtual Functions (VFs) não estiverem habilitadas, o plugin instala "
"e inicia um serviço systemd persistente no host. Este serviço escreve "
"``sriov_totalvfs`` em ``sriov_numvfs``, garantindo que as VFs permaneçam "
"habilitadas após reinicializações."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:321
msgid "Creates and autostarts the libvirt hostdev network on each host"
msgstr "Cria e inicia automaticamente a rede libvirt hostdev em cada host"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:322
msgid ""
"All SR-IOV networks that share the same Physical Function (PF) use a "
"single libvirt hostdev pool on each host. The total number of VMs across "
"all networks on that PF is limited by the total number of available VFs."
msgstr ""
"Todas as redes SR-IOV que compartilham a mesma Physical Function (PF) "
"utilizam um único pool libvirt hostdev em cada host. O número total de VMs "
"em todas as redes nessa PF é limitado pelo número total de VFs disponíveis."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:325
msgid "Creating the SR-IOV Network"
msgstr "Criando a Rede SR-IOV"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:328
msgid "Select :guilabel:`+ Add` > **HVM SR-IOV Network**"
msgstr "Selecione :guilabel:`+ Add` > **HVM SR-IOV Network**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:334
msgid "**Physical Function** — Select the SR-IOV capable NIC (PF)"
msgstr "**Physical Function** — Selecione a NIC compatível com SR-IOV (PF)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:335
msgid "**VLAN ID** — The VLAN for hardware-level VST tagging"
msgstr "**VLAN ID** — A VLAN para marcação VST em nível de hardware"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:340
msgid "Deleting an HVM Network"
msgstr "Excluindo uma Rede HVM"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:342
msgid ""
"Deleting an HVM network removes the network definition from all hosts in "
"the cluster and from the |morpheus| database."
msgstr ""
"Excluir uma rede HVM remove a definição de rede de todos os hosts do "
"cluster e do banco de dados do |morpheus|."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:345
msgid "Select the network to delete from the list"
msgstr "Selecione a rede a ser excluída na lista"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:346
msgid "Click the delete icon next to the network name"
msgstr "Clique no ícone de exclusão ao lado do nome da rede"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:349
msgid ""
"The system removes the libvirt network definition and its port group from"
" all hosts in the cluster. For Standard Networks, it removes trunk VLAN "
"IDs automatically along with the port group without requiring separate "
"cleanup. The system also updates the Aruba CX switch configuration for "
"the removed VLAN IDs through the Generic Integration."
msgstr ""
"O sistema remove a definição de rede libvirt e seu port group de todos os "
"hosts do cluster. Para Redes Standard, ele remove os IDs de VLAN trunk "
"automaticamente junto com o port group sem exigir limpeza separada. O "
"sistema também atualiza a configuração do switch Aruba CX para os IDs de "
"VLAN removidos por meio da Generic Integration."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/hvm_networks.rst:351
msgid ""
"For an Overlay Network, deletion also removes its dedicated OVS bridge "
"and VXLAN configuration from participating hosts. Move or disconnect "
"every VM first and verify no workload depends on the VNI; deleting the "
"network removes connectivity and does not migrate attached workloads."
msgstr ""
"Para uma Rede Overlay, a exclusão também remove sua bridge OVS dedicada e "
"a configuração VXLAN dos hosts participantes. Mova ou desconecte todas as "
"VMs primeiro e verifique se nenhuma carga de trabalho depende do VNI; "
